            <ArticleTitle>[Clinical aspects of cerebral arteriovenous malformations].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1153-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The incidence, site and clinical aspects of cerebral arteriovenous malformation (AVM) are examined with particular reference to symptoms like epilepsy and headache that enter into the differential diagnosis between this and other pathologies of the central nervous system. The clinical presentation of the AVM beside includes dementia-type syndromes and subarachnoid haemorrhage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
